{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor maintained a safe responsibility chain across the evolving episode: allergy/medication uncertainty was escalated to the ward/anesthesia team, red flags were repeatedly operationalized, results and medication changes were tied to formal hospital systems, and discharge/wound-care actions were made executable. The final family turn left a specific medication-confirmation question open, but the family already had pharmacy/written label instructions and the doctor had created a safe open loop with wound-clinic follow-up and return precautions. Two high-order points were completed with trajectory impact: targeted verification of possible topical-drug reaction versus infection/irritation, and dynamic reprioritization as the situation changed from pre-op review to surgery, negative-pressure care, drug-order clarification, and discharge planning. With no responsibility-chain error or important non-chain defect, this meets Perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00909",
        "explanation": "Doctor converted discharge into an executable checklist.",
        "quote": "总结一下您出院后的行动清单"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00909",
        "explanation": "Doctor specified professional wound-care timing and location rather than home self-management.",
        "quote": "按2-3天或“渗湿明显随时”的频率"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00909",
        "explanation": "Doctor gave emergency return boundary.",
        "quote": "一旦出现，立即返院"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00924",
        "explanation": "Family demonstrated receipt of pharmacy-labeled antibiotic instructions, leaving only a safe confirmation question open.",
        "quote": "药袋上写的是“头孢克肟分散片”"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "Valid open closure: the last family message asked for confirmation of a pharmacy-labeled oral antibiotic, but the responsible systems were already assigned to pharmacy/written discharge instructions and wound clinic, with clear no-home-dressing-change instructions and return precautions. The episode remained safe and traceable despite the final unanswered confirmation.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
